DoorDash is inviting U.S. customers to join a waitlist for an AI assistant that can take food orders through Apple's Messages app (via <a href="https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-09-30/doordash-unveils-text-to-order-ai-agent-that-works-with-apple-s-imessage"><em>Bloomberg</em></a>).<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/doordash.jpg" alt="" width="1672" height="941" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1067927" /><br/>
The phone number used in the conversation connects the request to a customer's DoorDash account. The assistant can use previous purchases and preferences to help put together an order, then use a saved payment method at checkout. Customers can also view food photos in the chat or send a picture of their fridge for recipe ideas and suggestions for missing ingredients.<br/>
<br/>
The service builds on <a href="https://about.doordash.com/en-us/news/ask-doordash">Ask DoorDash</a>, which launched inside the DoorDash app in June. DoorDash <a href="https://help.doordash.com/en-us/consumers/article/meet-your-new-ai-grocery-assistant">describes the message assistant</a> as a pilot for select U.S. account holders and advises users to check their carts before paying because the AI can make mistakes.<br/>
<br/>
To join the beta waitlist, U.S. iOS users can enter their phone number at <a href="https://www.doordash.com/text">doordash.com/text</a> and select Continue. DoorDash says Android support is coming soon.<br/>
